WEBVTT

00:00:00.306 --> 00:00:01.067
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:02.253 --> 00:00:04.280
<v><b>A:</b></v> Right, just leaving home now.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:07.074
<v><b>B:</b></v> Oh great. What’s your ETA?

00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:09.720
<v><b>A:</b></v> Around 6, 6.30 I’d say.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.963
<v><b>B:</b></v> See you then.

00:00:13.716 --> 00:00:14.465
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:16.812 --> 00:00:21.192
<v><b>A:</b></v> Excuse me, you haven’t seen Mr Knightley’s PA anywhere, have you?

00:00:21.272 --> 00:00:25.813
<v><b>B:</b></v> Sorry, he seems to have gone AWOL. I haven’t seen him since early this morning.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:29.707
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:30.876 --> 00:00:33.212
<v><b>A:</b></v> What happened to that report you were going to finish?

00:00:33.411 --> 00:00:37.456
<v><b>B:</b></v> OMG, I completely forgot about it! Sorry, I’ll do it ASAP.

00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:41.497
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:42.814 --> 00:00:46.668
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> HIV continues to be a major global public health issue,

00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:49.405
especially in East and Southern Africa.

00:00:49.838 --> 00:00:56.092
Since the start of the epidemic, an estimated 88.4 million people have become infected

00:00:56.157 --> 00:01:02.204
with the virus, and 42.3 million have died of AIDS-related illnesses.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:06.399
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:01:08.356 --> 00:01:10.410
<v><b>A:</b></v> What do you think of your local MP?

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.650
<v><b>B:</b></v> Well, I didn’t vote for her, but she’s OK I suppose.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:19.546
She’s well qualified, she has a degree in law and an MBA, but I don’t really agree with her politics.